    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0590" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-27T11:00:00+09:00">June 27, 1948—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 27—1:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1163. Reference paragraph 5, Deptel 920 of June 24, Embtel 1149 of June 25 and
                    Deptel 892 of June 17. Revised article IV (old numbering) of bilateral aid
                    agreement as agreed with Lapham mission was presented by <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> to Foreign Office June 25. Full text contained in
                    Embassy’s immediately following telegram.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d477-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office brusquely rejected proposal by <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> June 26 as “undesirable <pb facs="0591" n="581"
                        xml:id="pg581"/> and unnecessary” and “creates impression that
                    administrative integrity of China is not strictly respected”.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1163, repeated Shanghai 534.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
